     6	Run:  python -m cma.mcp_server
     7	
     8	Files: tools only read files under CMA_DATA_DIR, which must be set (MCP hosts often
     9	start servers with the working directory at / or ~, so there is no default), and only
    10	.csv statements and .yaml/.yml policies. A refused statement is reported by line
    11	number only; cell values are never echoed to the client.
    12	
    13	Descriptions: statement descriptions are text the payer chose ("IGNORE PREVIOUS
    14	INSTRUCTIONS..."), and an MCP client is a model, so no tool ever returns one (R34).
    15	`transactions_for` still accepts include_descriptions, and says the text was withheld.
    16	
    17	Offline lock: the server is a way for data to reach a model, so while offline_lock is on
    18	in firm.yaml (the default) it refuses to start, however it is started (main(), or an
    19	embedding script calling `server.run()`, an async runner or an ASGI app), and every tool
    20	refuses before reading a file. firm.yaml is read on each start and each call.
